# Commenting Principles

## Philosophy

Code should be self-documenting. Comments explain **why**, not **what**.

## Three levels of comments

### 1. Module header (required for every file in `shared/lib/`)

```typescript
/**
 * Unified notification service.
 *
 * Three runtimes:
 * - Electron → ipcRenderer (native OS notifications)
 * - PWA/Browser → Web Notifications API
 *
 * Usage:
 *   import { notificationService } from "~/shared/lib/notifications";
 *   await notificationService.show({ title: "New message", body: "Hello!" });
 */
```

Format: `/**` JSDoc, first line — what the module does, then key details, usage example.

Required for: `shared/lib/*.ts`, `entities/*/*.model.ts`, `shared/api/*.ts`, `i18n/index.ts`.
Not needed for: `*.ui.tsx` components (component name = documentation), `*.types.ts`, `index.ts` barrel files.

### 2. Section separator (for files >100 lines)

```typescript
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Types
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
```

Separates logical blocks in long files. 75 characters wide, one word/phrase.

### 3. Inline comment (only when non-obvious)

```typescript
// BAD_EVENT_QUEUE_ID: server restarted, queue expired — re-register
if (result.code === "BAD_EVENT_QUEUE_ID") {
```

## What to comment

| Situation | Comment needed? | Example |
|----------|----------------|--------|
| Non-obvious business logic | ✅ Yes | `// Zulip API: 100=Owner, 200=Admin (not the other way around!)` |
| Workaround or hack | ✅ Yes | `// Workaround: tinyexec exports .mjs but package.json declares .js` |
| Why a specific approach was chosen | ✅ Yes | `// Long-poll fetch is not throttled in background tabs (unlike setTimeout)` |
| Edge case handling | ✅ Yes | `// DM key may be invalid if userId is not yet loaded` |
| What a function does | ❌ JSDoc header | Function name should be self-documenting |
| What a line of code does | ❌ No | `const count = items.length; // get count` — NEVER |
| Imports | ❌ No | Do not comment import lines |
| Obvious operations | ❌ No | `set({ loading: true }); // set loading to true` — NEVER |

## What NOT to comment

```typescript
// ❌ Narrative (explains what, not why)
// Set the user name
const name = user.full_name;

// ❌ Journal-style (who, when changed)
// Added by @developer on 2026-03-13
// Fixed bug #123

// ❌ Commented-out code
// const oldValue = computeOld();
// if (oldValue) { ... }

// ❌ Separators without content
// ================================
// END OF FILE
// ================================
```

## JSDoc format for exported functions

For **public API** functions in `shared/lib/`:

```typescript
/** Sanitizes HTML from Zulip messages. Strips unsafe tags, rewrites relative image URLs. */
export function sanitizeHtml(html: string, baseUrl?: string): string {
```

One line if the function is simple. Multi-line JSDoc if:
- There are non-obvious parameters
- Important side effects
- Throws specific errors

